examples.question_text:
Estimate each marked angle.
(a) Compare with half a right angle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\draw[black] (V)--(0:3);
\draw[black] (V)--(38:3);
\draw[black] (0:0.65) arc (0:38:0.65);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) Compare with a right angle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\draw[black] (V)--(0:3);
\draw[black] (V)--(99:3);
\draw[black] (0:0.65) arc (0:99:0.65);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Estimate the marked angle. Compare it with a right angle and a straight angle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\draw[black] (V)--(0:3);
\draw[black] (V)--(132:3);
\draw[black] (0:0.65) arc (0:132:0.65);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Estimate the marked angle to the nearest $10^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\draw[black] (V)--(0:3);
\draw[black] (V)--(168:3);
\draw[black] (0:0.65) arc (0:168:0.65);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Estimate the marked reflex angle using $180^{\circ}$, $270^{\circ}$ and $360^{\circ}$ as benchmarks.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\draw[black] (V)--(35:3);
\draw[black] (V)--(109:3);
\draw[black] (109:0.75) arc (109:395:0.75);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Estimate the marked reflex angle using $270^{\circ}$ and $360^{\circ}$ as benchmarks.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\draw[black] (V)--(0:3);
\draw[black] (V)--(65:3);
\draw[black] (65:0.75) arc (65:360:0.75);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) An angle is just wider than a right angle. Is $100^{\circ}$ or $170^{\circ}$ a more sensible estimate?

Estimate the marked angle. You may turn the picture mentally to compare it with a familiar benchmark.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\draw[black] (V)--(150:3);
\draw[black] (V)--(179:3);
\draw[black] (150:0.65) arc (150:179:0.65);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Estimate the marked angle to the nearest $10^{\circ}$. Compare it with half a right angle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\draw[black] (V)--(0:3);
\draw[black] (V)--(56:3);
\draw[black] (0:0.65) arc (0:56:0.65);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) An angle is a little less than half a right angle. Is $40^{\circ}$ or $80^{\circ}$ a more sensible estimate?
(c) An angle is a little more than half a right angle. Give a sensible estimate.
